#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Kulan Fleet: the administrator's app for Kulan OS fleet management.

Signs in to the kulan-fleet Supabase project with an email and a one-time
code (no password), keeps the session in the GNOME keyring, and talks only
to the fleet-admin function, which shows nothing unless the signed-in email
is on the fleet's admin list. Everything the computers report comes from
the fleet server; nothing here can run commands on them beyond the actions
Kulan OS allows. Erasing a computer only works when its own user allowed it
there and its disk is encrypted, and needs the computer's name typed to
confirm. Every change is kept in the organisation's activity log.

People: the accounts on the organisation's computers. A new person (or one
who forgot their password) gets a setup code made here, on this computer:
only its one-way hash (yescrypt, or SHA-512 crypt) goes to the server, and
the code is shown once for the admin to hand over. At the sign-in screen
they type it and choose their own password straight away.

  kulan-fleet-admin              open the app
  kulan-fleet-admin --self-test  build every page with sample data (no network)
"""
